thag18.1:4.1 starts: Coming down from my dwelling place,
thag18.1:4.2 starts: I entered the city for alms,
thag18.1:4.3 starts: stood courteously next to a leper
thag18.1:4.4 starts: eating his meal.
thag18.1:6.1 starts: Sitting next to a wall,
thag18.1:6.2 starts: I ate that morsel of food,
thag18.1:6.3 starts: and neither while eating it,
thag18.1:6.4 starts: did I feel
thag18.1:7.1 starts: Whoever has mastered
thag18.1:7.2 starts: left-over scraps for food,
thag18.1:7.3 starts: smelly urine for medicine,
thag18.1:7.4 starts: the foot of a tree for a dwelling,
thag18.1:7.5 starts: cast-off rags for robes:
thag18.1:7.6 starts: He is a man
thag18.1:8.1 starts: Where some are exhausted
thag18.1:8.2 starts: climbing the mountain,
thag18.1:8.3 starts: there
thag18.1:8.4 starts: the Awakened One’s heir
thag18.1:8.5 starts: —mindful, alert,
thag18.1:8.6 starts: buoyed by his psychic power—
thag18.1:21.1 starts: There is no such pleasure for me
thag18.1:21.2 starts: in the music of a five-piece band
thag18.1:21.3 starts: as there is when my mind
thag18.1:21.4 starts: seeing the Dhamma
thag18.1:25.1 starts: Not better,
thag18.1:25.2 starts: he thinks himself better,
thag18.1:25.3 starts: The wise don’t praise him,
thag18.1:25.4 starts: the stiff-necked man.
thag18.1:30.1 starts: A monk conceited & vain,
thag18.1:30.2 starts: even though clad
thag18.1:30.3 starts: like a monkey in a lion’s skin,
thag18.1:30.4 starts: doesn’t shine because of it.
thag18.1:35.1 starts: ‘How very amazing:
thag18.1:35.2 starts: the awakened ones’
thag18.1:35.3 starts: of which we have no direct knowledge,
thag18.1:35.4 starts: though we have come
thag18.1:36.1 starts: Seeing Sāriputta,
thag18.1:36.2 starts: a man worthy of worship,
thag18.1:36.3 starts: worshipped by deva retinues,
thag18.1:36.4 starts: Kappina
thig1.11:1.1 starts: So freed! So thoroughly freed am I!—
thig1.11:1.2 starts: from three crooked things set free:
thig1.11:1.3 starts: from mortar, pestle,
thig1.11:1.4 starts: & crooked old husband.
thig1.11:1.5 starts: Having uprooted the craving
thig1.11:1.6 starts: I’m from aging & death set free.
thig3.5:3.1 starts: Today—with arrow removed,
thig3.5:3.2 starts: without hunger, entirely
thig3.5:3.3 starts: to the Buddha, Dhamma, & Saṅgha I go,
thig3.5:3.4 starts: for refuge to
